> The difference bwn predict.ergmbysim and predict.ergm is that:
>
> predict.ergmbysim compute the probabilities like you said. AS the
> proportion of links to 1 in a large number of simulated networks.
>
> predict.ergm does not simulate anything. It compute the differences
> delta(y_ij), and p_ij is the conditional probability, as in the
> pseudolikelihood approch.

It is clear for me now, thanks.


~michal

