Hi Jeff,

The "istar" term does not have a "base" argument (according to the manual page for it). That is what is causing the error. However, e.g.,

  summary(samplike ~ edges + istar(3, "group"))
        edges istar3.group
           88           96

says there are 96 three in-stars where all three vertices have the same "group".

For question 2, I would write a simple loop that extracts a matrix of all triangles from the edge-list as a three column matrix of vertex ids. Then you can analyze all patterns as 
functions of attributes of the vertices. While there is no pre-packaged function to do this, it is straightforward to write.

Cheers,

Mark	

