Dear List members,

I have a question that probably is easy to answer, but I was not able to find a clear answer, neither in 

Hunter DR, Handcock MS, Butts CT, Goodreau SM, Morris M (2008b). ergm: A Package to Fit, Simulate and Diagnose Exponential-Family Models for Networks. Journal of Statistical Software, 24(3).

nor elsewhere. It concerns the interpretation of the absdiff effect.

If I have a metric attribute (like size of company), and my model goes as follows:

model <- ergm(net ~ edges + absdiff("size"))

what does it mean when I get a significant positive, a significant negative or no significant coefficient. Since the term uses the difference a significant positive effect should imply a heterophily of for the size of companies. So companies have a tendency to collaborate, when there size is different, am I right? A significant negative effect then, should indicate homophily. No significant effect would mean, there is no special pattern. Is the interpretation the same for directed and undirected network?
Sorry for posing such a beginners question 
kind regards
richard


